# blog.zd — a static blog, modelled on the milestone-7 portfolio target.
#
# ⚠️ ASPIRATIONAL, and it found a blocking gap. Exercises three designs
# that are specified but unimplemented: the `static` placement
# (§14C.3b), the FFI (§14E), and `record` declarations (§14B.1).
#
# Writing it revealed that ZDeceptron HAS NO STANDARD LIBRARY (§14F).
# Three things below were invented and existed in no spec:
#   - `contains`      no text operations were defined at all
#   - `readMarkdown`  `static` did not specify how files are read
#   - `is ""`         worked, but there was no `isEmpty` or `length`
# Two of the three have since landed. `contains`, `length of` and `is ""`
# are all in `crates/zdc-lib/prelude/`, and so is what this file could not
# ask for at all: `before with value is body, delimiter is newline` and
# `withoutPrefix with value is heading, prefix is "# "` are the title, and
# `withoutSuffix with value is (afterLast with value is path, delimiter is
# "/"), suffix is ".md"` is the slug — so `Post.title` and `Post.slug` are
# derivable from a file rather than being fields somebody has to hand-write.
# `readMarkdown` remains invented.
# The rest is left in deliberately: this file documents what a real program
# needs, which is more useful than a version trimmed to what compiles.
#
# Note what this program does NOT need: no `server` placement, no
# `durable` placement, no identity, no database, no API. A blog is a
# `client` + `static` application, and that is why it is reachable.

use "./layout" for PageShell, PostCard

record Post
    slug      is Text
    title     is Text
    body      is Text
    published is Whole
    draft     is Truth

# `marked` is pure computation with no environmental dependency, so it is
# `anywhere` — it may be called from client or static context alike.
foreign renderMarkdown is anywhere
    from  "marked" as "parse"
    takes source is Text
    gives Text

# Read at compile time and inlined into the bundle. Because no boundary
# is crossed at runtime, this is `List of Post` — not `Remote of List of
# Post`. Rule 1 is satisfied rather than excepted.
state posts is static List of Post from readMarkdown "content/blog"

# Derived at build time from build-time data: still static, still free.
state published is static List of Post from onlyPublished with posts

function onlyPublished with all
    from all
    keep each post where not post.draft
    sort each post by post.published

# Client state: the reader's filter box. Lost on reload, which is correct.
state query is client Text starting ""

view
    PageShell "Writing"
        Input query, hint is "filter posts"

        each post in published
            if post.title contains query or query is ""
                PostCard post.slug, title is post.title
                    Text renderMarkdown with source is post.body
